    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "[nums[i], nums[j]] = [nums[j], nums[i]];   // destructuring does it in one line"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "nums[i], nums[j] = nums[j], nums[i]        # tuple swap does it in one line"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int temp = nums[i];\nnums[i] = nums[j];\nnums[j] = temp;"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "swap(nums[i], nums[j]);                    // std::swap"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Reversing in place"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Swap the first and last elements, then the second and second-to-last, moving inward until the two indexes meet. About n / 2 swaps, no extra array."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function reverse(nums) {\n  for (let l = 0, r = nums.length - 1; l < r; l++, r--) {\n    [nums[l], nums[r]] = [nums[r], nums[l]];\n  }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def reverse(nums):\n    l, r = 0, len(nums) - 1\n    while l < r:\n        nums[l], nums[r] = nums[r], nums[l]\n        l += 1\n        r -= 1"
